{
  "_what": "The tier every one of Uber Base's 92 component sets was placed in, as DATA. docs/BASELINE.md states the tier counts in prose; this is what a machine reads. Parsing the prose was tried and leaked - a substring match put \"Message card\" in tier 2 because \"Message card - Carousel\" is in tier 2, and the deferred tier is described by category rather than by set name, so it matched nothing.",
  "_how": "Derived from vendor/uber-base-keys.json (the harvest) plus the four tier lists below. tests/skills.test.js asserts every set has exactly one tier, that no set is unassigned, and that the counts and variant sums are what BASELINE.md claims.",
  "_tiers": {
    "tier1": "A SaaS surface needs it and site-factory had no answer. All 17 settled: 16 redrawn on the `Base (redrawn)` page, Typography taken as the ten-step ramp.",
    "tier2": "Real but not load-bearing for a data surface. Two carry `Beta` in their own name, which is Base telling you not to depend on them yet.",
    "deferred": "Every Date picker and Time picker set, plus the mobile-only grabber. Deferred, not rejected: a date picker is the highest-effort, highest-risk control in any system and there are good accessible implementations to adopt. Base needs its own because Uber ships in 70 countries.",
    "answered": "Already covered by a site-factory block, named in the `answeredBy` field. Both systems converged on the same controls because the controls are the part that is not optional."
  },
